110 {\cf20 /*}\par
111 {\cf20   These functions compress data in successive blocks of any size,}\par
112 {\cf20   using previous blocks as dictionary, to improve compression ratio.}\par
113 {\cf20   One key assumption is that previous blocks (up to 64 KB) remain read-accessible while compressing next blocks.}\par
114 {\cf20   There is an exception for ring buffers, which can be smaller than 64 KB.}\par
115 {\cf20   Ring-buffer scenario is automatically detected and handled within LZ4_compress_HC_continue().}\par
116 {\cf20 }\par
117 {\cf20   Before starting compression, state must be allocated and properly initialized.}\par
118 {\cf20   LZ4_createStreamHC() does both, though compression level is set to LZ4HC_CLEVEL_DEFAULT.}\par
119 {\cf20 }\par
120 {\cf20   Selecting the compression level can be done with LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast() (starts a new stream)}\par
121 {\cf20   or LZ4_setCompressionLevel() (anytime, between blocks in the same stream) (experimental).}\par
122 {\cf20   LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast() only works on states which have been properly initialized at least once,}\par
123 {\cf20   which is automatically the case when state is created using LZ4_createStreamHC().}\par
124 {\cf20 }\par
125 {\cf20   After reset, a first "fictional block" can be designated as initial dictionary,}\par
126 {\cf20   using LZ4_loadDictHC() (Optional).}\par
127 {\cf20 }\par
128 {\cf20   Invoke LZ4_compress_HC_continue() to compress each successive block.}\par
129 {\cf20   The number of blocks is unlimited.}\par
130 {\cf20   Previous input blocks, including initial dictionary when present,}\par
131 {\cf20   must remain accessible and unmodified during compression.}\par
132 {\cf20 }\par
133 {\cf20   It's allowed to update compression level anytime between blocks,}\par
134 {\cf20   using LZ4_setCompressionLevel() (experimental).}\par
135 {\cf20 }\par
136 {\cf20   'dst' buffer should be sized to handle worst case scenarios}\par
137 {\cf20   (see LZ4_compressBound(), it ensures compression success).}\par
138 {\cf20   In case of failure, the API does not guarantee recovery,}\par
139 {\cf20   so the state _must_ be reset.}\par
140 {\cf20   To ensure compression success}\par
141 {\cf20   whenever `dst` buffer size cannot be made >= LZ4_compressBound(),}\par
142 {\cf20   consider using LZ4_compress_HC_continue_destSize().}\par
143 {\cf20 }\par
144 {\cf20   Whenever previous input blocks can't be preserved unmodified in-place during compression of next blocks,}\par
145 {\cf20   it's possible to copy the last blocks into a more stable memory space, using LZ4_saveDictHC().}\par
146 {\cf20   Return value of LZ4_saveDictHC() is the size of dictionary effectively saved into 'safeBuffer' (<= 64 KB)}\par
147 {\cf20 }\par
148 {\cf20   After completing a streaming compression,}\par
149 {\cf20   it's possible to start a new stream of blocks, using the same LZ4_streamHC_t state,}\par
150 {\cf20   just by resetting it, using LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast().}\par
151 {\cf20 */}\par
152 \par
153 LZ4LIB_API {\cf18 void} LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast(LZ4_streamHC_t* streamHCPtr, {\cf18 int} compressionLevel);   {\cf20 /* v1.9.0+ */}\par
